{"step_index":51,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:17:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T18:47:45+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T18:47:55+05:30\nThe search for \"Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B MMLU-Pro MATH GPQA benchmark scores vs Claude Opus\" returned the following summary:\nAs of August 2026, benchmark data for these models reflects the following performance landscape. Please note that \"Claude Opus\" refers to the current generation of Anthropic’s flagship models (e.g., Opus 5, 4.8), while NVIDIA's **Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B** (released June 2026) is positioned as a high-performance open-weight model[1][2][3].\n\n### Benchmark Performance Overview\n\n| Benchmark | Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B | Claude Opus (Flagship Versions) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **MMLU-Pro** | Generally ranges 81%–88%[4] | ~89%–92%[5][6][7] |\n| **GPQA (Diamond)** | ~86.7%[8] | ~94%–95%[2] |\n| **MATH** | Competitive (Strong reasoning)[4] | State-of-the-art frontier performance[9] |\n\n---\n\n### Key Contextual Differences\n\n*   **MMLU-Pro:** This benchmark, which uses 10 answer options and deeper reasoning requirements, is currently dominated by the latest proprietary frontier models[10][11]. While Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B demonstrates very strong capabilities (with specific versions scoring in the high 80s)[4], recent iterations of Claude Opus (e.g., Opus 5) consistently lead the leaderboard, often exceeding 91%[7].\n*   **GPQA (Graduate-Level Google-Proof Q&A):** This is widely considered one of the most difficult benchmarks for current LLMs[12][13]. Claude Opus models have maintained a significant lead here, with scores frequently reaching the mid-90s in recent testing[2]. Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B performs well for an open-weight model (approx. 86.7%)[8] but generally trails the leading proprietary frontier models in this specific category[2].\n*   **Architecture & Usage:** \n    *   **Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B** is an open-weight, hybrid Mamba-Transformer Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model[4][3]. Its primary value proposition is high inference throughput, cost-efficiency for enterprise deployment, and \"agentic\" control, making it highly suitable for pipelines where developers need speed and the ability to run models on their own infrastructure[14][3].\n    *   **Claude Opus** remains a proprietary, closed-source flagship model[2]. It is typically favored for tasks requiring the absolute highest level of reasoning, nuanced instruction following, and complex multi-step analysis where proprietary model performance is the priority[9][2].\n\n**Summary:** While Nemotron-3 Ultra 550B is among the most capable open-weight models available and competes closely with many top-tier systems, the latest Claude Opus versions currently hold a performance advantage on standardized knowledge and reasoning benchmarks like MMLU-Pro and GPQA[2][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [openrouter.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrUSAQCK1R_7PiVgvU90S-J4-lEL7JOLJ9tDvGDc10PEqdMadYP9ZipxVAjlvQUeKGF1Mep_7qpM9Rf7tCw6fk6wYn9LpQk6ESdbcOqw6FR6-tnpelESiUZFNesdpERlti3cacQ_I8Csi_4h8S)\n[2] [vellum.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGXbDDVdblPN5iHjRnqk8vy7JtfhTvkaC-6PfekGWbbyqXnBJYjy6UVOdyr-umV3i9JedlOpAGy4LaoM0-w7DPAL6OSm2rwN-8Ku3KOMuzeen-y9DNtfJKe0Kck)\n[3] [nvidia.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE2AFDunJyIVhUlYBeZQsS0IR_VibBz0FxjsqJ__wWjm26TgAQu1FGGF2z7bOJo1-rHSr8h_HstGhmr7R8sXqr424fd8aXjq5NWQJKzffbxRe78hYyYuZ4NxTCp66RynBSibkt8uFPuxWznyA_uDzsW6w==)\n[4] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGUcrqcMqNfMk19n_2CYgWBG4Sd28eUTKsWB1V2FWf5YnaVy0eQrtVCb0B_jGHpFtNyGwVISeibNKhkDj9ETme8X42G8D5wdcRZisW7yFkArKeJDYqcEO07w_drrkYNfUU0QbMCeSw8zv4nJVdG_ZvrTMJewsk_YFOiQw==)\n[5] [artificialanalysis.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH0-6fY8XQuViC7igbeT1fJQQhCYoIRS5KDDt-MrwHxPtL56hjMql5q6I