{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:17:55Z","content":"Got all the data. Here's the straight comparison:\n\n---\n\n### Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B — What It Actually Is\n\n| Spec | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Maker** | NVIDIA (not some random person — a \\$3 trillion company) |\n| **Released** | June 4, 2026 |\n| **Parameters** | 550B total, **55B active** per token (MoE architecture) |\n| **Context** | 1M tokens ✅ |\n| **Open-weight** | Yes — you can self-host it |\n| **Free API** | Yes, via OpenRouter (rate-limited) |\n\nThis is a **legitimate** model from a major lab. Unlike OX Alpha, there's full transparency.\n\n---\n\n### The Head-to-Head Comparison\n\n#### Coding Benchmarks\n\n| Benchmark | Opus 4.6 | Nemotron 3 Ultra | Opus 5 |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **SWE-bench Verified** | 80.8% | **71.9%** | ~92%+ |\n| **DeepSWE** | ~54% | — | **74.0%** |\n| **LiveCodeBench** | — | 89.0% | — |\n| **Terminal Bench 2.0** | — | 56.4% | — |\n\n#### Knowledge & Reasoning\n\n| Benchmark | Opus 4.6 | Nemotron 3 Ultra | Opus 5 |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **MMLU-Pro** | ~85-87% | ~81-88% | ~91-92% |\n| **GPQA Diamond** | ~78-82% | **86.7%** | ~94-95% |\n| **HumanEval** | ~90%+ | 88.4% | ~95%+ |\n\n---\n\n### What This Means — No BS\n\n**Nemotron 3 Ultra vs Opus 4.6 (yours):**\n- Nemotron **loses** on SWE-bench Verified (71.9% vs 80.8%)\n- Nemotron **wins** on GPQA Diamond (86.7% vs ~80%) — graduate-level science questions\n- They're roughly **comparable** on MMLU-Pro and HumanEval\n- Nemotron has a **1M context window** — that's a real advantage for large codebases\n\n**Nemotron 3 Ultra vs Opus 5:**\n- Opus 5 **dominates everything**. 92%+ SWE-bench, 94% GPQA, 91% MMLU-Pro. Not close.\n\n**But here's the thing that actually matters for you:**\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Is Nemotron free? | Yes — legitimately free via API, and you can self-host |\n| Is it from a real company? | Yes — NVIDIA, not some anonymous stealth account |\n| Is it transparent? | Yes — open weights, published benchmarks, technical paper |\n| Does it beat Opus 4.6? | **Mixed** — wins some, loses some. Roughly same tier |\n| Does it beat Opus 5? | **No** — Opus 5 is clearly ahead on nearly everything |\n| Is it worth using? | **Yes, for specific use cases** (see below) |\n\n### When Nemotron 3 Ultra Actually Makes Sense\n\n- ✅ You need **1M context** (massive documents, full codebases)\n- ✅ You want **free + transparent** (real company, open weights, known data policies)\n- ✅ You're doing **agentic pipelines** — it's optimized for long-running autonomous tasks\n- ✅ You care about **data privacy** — you can literally run it on your own hardware\n\n### When to Stick with Opus\n\n- ✅ **Precise bug-fixing** — Opus 4.6 still beats it on SWE-bench (80.8% vs 71.9%)\n- ✅ **You need the absolute best** — Opus 5 crushes everything\n- ✅ **Creative/writing tasks** — Opus models are generally better for nuanced writing\n\n### Bottom Line vs OX Alpha\n\nNemotron 3 Ultra is what a **legitimate free model** looks like — published by NVIDIA, open weights, documented benchmarks, clear data policies. Compare that to OX Alpha's anonymous stealth launch with cherry-picked numbers. Night and day in credibility, roughly similar in actual performance (~63% vs ~71.9% on coding benchmarks)."}
