{"step_index":55,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:22:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T18:52:19+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T18:52:26+05:30\nThe search for \"Gemini 3.1 Pro benchmark SWE-bench verified MMLU GPQA DeepSWE 2026\" returned the following summary:\nGemini 3.1 Pro is a flagship reasoning model from Google DeepMind, released in preview on **February 19, 2026**[1][2]. It was designed as a focused intelligence upgrade, marking the first time Google used a \".1\" version increment, and is built to excel at complex, multi-step problem-solving[3][1][2].\n\n### Key Benchmark Performance\nAt the time of its release, Gemini 3.1 Pro showed significant improvements in core reasoning benchmarks compared to its predecessor, Gemini 3 Pro[4][5].\n\n| Benchmark | Gemini 3.1 Pro Score | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **SWE-Bench Verified** | **80.6%** | A competitive score in agentic coding tasks[6][5]. |\n| **GPQA Diamond** | **94.3%** | Evaluates graduate-level scientific knowledge[6][5]. |\n| **MMLU** | **92.6%** | Measures multitask language understanding[6]. |\n| **ARC-AGI-2** | **77.1%** | A significant jump from Gemini 3 Pro (31.1%)[6][5]. |\n\n*Note: While Gemini 3.1 Pro is highly capable, the AI benchmarking landscape in 2026 has become increasingly competitive, with newer models and specialized agents frequently updating the standings across various metrics[7][8].*\n\n### Context on Other Benchmarks\n*   **DeepSWE:** This is a distinct benchmark designed to measure frontier coding agents on original, long-horizon engineering tasks[9][10]. Unlike some traditional coding benchmarks, it emphasizes tasks written from scratch to reduce contamination[10][11]. As of August 2026, newer flagship models (such as Claude Opus 5 and GPT-5.6 Sol) have set the pace on the DeepSWE leaderboard[8][12].\n*   **Benchmark Evolution:** By mid-2026, benchmarks like MMLU have become functionally saturated, shifting the focus of evaluations toward more specialized metrics like **Terminal-Bench** (for CLI-based coding), **MCP Atlas** (for tool orchestration), and **DeepSWE** (for long-horizon software engineering)[7][8].\n\n### Model Features\n*   **Reasoning Depth:** A major introduction with the 3.1 series is the ability to set \"Thinking\" levels (Low, Medium, High) per request, allowing developers to balance cost, speed, and reasoning depth[3][1].\n*   **Capacity:** The model retains a 1 million token context window and supports multimodal inputs including text, audio, images, video, and PDFs[6][13][14].\n*   **Positioning:** Gemini 3.1 Pro is positioned between the efficient Gemini \"Flash\" models and the more specialized, research-oriented \"Deep Think\" tier[3][1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [chatlyai.app](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFSEfJ9xO3YCH9h9ufPTKJC-GN_LZs9I6XqjmckHXEW9clNuqN5zLCYSncbR2m4vEzqAPVb-6Ocx2eQDgld5GtI3Ao5Lt2YPbtm7AygMcHdVL6_Jea9JO4xNvddkUb44rGNptGUdC0t)\n[2] [datacamp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGRiEX9Nbo3DMbfbjypeYlJFGbjZRLzPt2G6m6DIjfmTDQj9q-7x1Skxhd1IYq1NaXxzgbD4mqV01BHn6oJt_6CAXQx5UrUi0Up-FWhR5IbFo9gj-9-CVofZAQ74EEz)\n[3] [nxcode.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGAQVaB5pjS5ljHKi8hv172ANA0RLGu6bLdbHvIHnJYFthFGgEpY5gANVHz2MgsVCh5uOyeDhxtSJHkkmxihdtnl9XFjPoW89K_P2Tmm4yWEnZ9fmfSmG-mBHp58jArDxsBQkXk4cooeuvbhKswoJromXPQMW61X3CJzxItC_jovM4YVbL8c2lWIbiQvPot1xDNpfeb)\n[4] [blog.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHVMJOb4JpItSEZYYUAL2wn6NjYQPtZF9Utm317j1jhosPjFSJ3Xq--4rri_vS1b6xQzbd4O_T6QFMzDhQkDCo8VptrrXamyHf_Kmox_7ylU9iAt0I-ETgjKM47so5YtON9z86-liT_v2krcSrinPDpEOD1feAVhuW4oebDIsKsdJOTIPWEtL13cHVdRw=)\n[5] [deepmind.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEYDQq-sK3WLZllVLDRp79ivwR9upiGmYsRp7UIGXeTyIGFjmLTuL5ETmUhF6HPaSh39CSAjkDLydN9fYgc4pdlEofRExpxyGG-CSvNTtG1qWkDlNmFQsE84fM_A2mhM6