{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:26:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T18:56:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T18:56:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/priyanshu%20readme/youtube/Stickman/implementation_plan.md`\nTotal Lines: 245\nTotal Bytes: 10157\nShowing lines 1 to 245\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Execution Plan v3 — Updated Aug 18, 2026\n2: \n3: > All previous versions had wrong assumptions. This one aligns with your actual corrections.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## What Changed From v2\n8: \n9: | v2 (Wrong) | v3 (Fixed) |\n10: |---|---|\n11: | Both channels from Day 1 | **Stickman scripts FIRST**, Nishchay study parallel, Nishchay production later |\n12: | Whop = find clients, cold DMs | Whop = community marketplace. Join, pick up RPM deals, clip, upload. |\n13: | Filled in niche details | **No niche plans given yet.** Plan waits for your input. |\n14: | 30-day monetization math | Removed. Don't bring up unless asked. |\n15: | Voice cloning recommendation | Deleted. |\n16: | 20-step daily plans | ADHD-friendly: next 1-2 actions only. |\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## The Sequence (Your Decision — Don't Rearrange)\n21: \n22: ```\n23: PHASE 1 (NOW):     Stickman → ideas, competitor study, scripts\n24: PHASE 1b (PARALLEL): Nishchay → READ competitor scripts (study only, no production)\n25: PHASE 2 (AFTER):   Nishchay → production begins once study phase improves your scripting\n26: ONGOING:           Clipping (Whop + Vyro) → see clipping/ folder for details\n27: ```\n28: \n29: **Split: 60% Stickman / 40% Nishchay**\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## Production Pipeline (Per Video — End to End)\n34: \n35: ### Step-by-Step Workflow\n36: \n37: ```\n38: Step 1: TOPIC VALIDATION\n39:     → Check project_brief.md in youtube/Stickman/projects/[NN]_[name]/\n40:     → vidIQ keyword validation (check competition score)\n41:     → vidIQ title scoring (aim for 85+, front-load emotion words)\n42:     → Confirm topic from phase1 deep research rankings\n43: \n44: Step 2: RESEARCH (Day 1)\n45:     → Read phase1_part1 or part2 for topic's deep research\n46:     → Watch 2-3 competitor reference videos\n47:     → Compile facts and sources into research_notes.md\n48: \n49: Step 3: SCRIPT (Day 1-2)\n50:     → Use /prompt-forge to write a tight scripting prompt for the AI\n51:     → Write hook (first 30 seconds — pattern interrupt)\n52:     → Full draft (~1,800 words for 12 min)\n53:     → While writing: activate /humanizer + /ai-writing-gaps + /stop-slop\n54:       (these run DURING writing, not as separate passes)\n55:     → /humanizer: kills surface AI tells (vocabulary, em dashes, rule-of-three)\n56:     → /ai-writing-gaps: fixes structural problems (pacing, sources, contrast)\n57:     → /stop-slop: removes predictable AI patterns from prose\n58:     → Save as script_v1.md in project folder\n59: \n60: Step 4: VOICEOVER (Day 2)\n61:     → ElevenLabs generation with emotional tags\n62:     → Save voiceover_notes.md\n63: \n64: Step 5: VISUALS (Day 2-3)\n65:     → Nano Banana 2 image generation per scene\n66:     → Google Omni video clips where needed\n67:     → Visual plan saved as visual_plan.md\n68: \n69: Step 6: ASSEMBLY (Day 3)\n70:     → Remotion/FFmpeg composition\n71:     → Captions added\n72:     → 4K export (local or GitHub Actions)\n73: \n74: Step 7: POLISH & PUBLISH (Day 3)\n75:     → Thumbnail designed (3 concepts, pick best)\n76:     → Title + description + tags finalized (vidIQ scored)\n77:     → vidIQ tag optimization (use volume-proven tags, avoid 0-vol keywords)\n78:     → vidIQ description template with timestamps\n79:     → Upload to YouTube\n80:     → Update project_brief.md checklist\n81: ```\n82: \n83: ## Updated Video Priority Order (Phase 1 Deep Research — Aug 17, 2026)\n84: \n85: | Priority | Topic | Composite Score | Project Folder |\n86: |----------|-------|:-:|----------------|\n87: | **Video 1** | The Most Terrifying Weapons Ever Banned | 94 (title: 93) | `projects/01_banned_weapons/` |\n88: | **Video 2** | Every Banned Book in History Explained | 83 | `projects/02_banned_books/` |\n89: | **Video 3** | Dumb War Tactics That Actually Worked | 74 | `projects/03_dumb_war_tactics/` |\n90: | **Video 4** | Every Monster from Greek Mythology Explained | 89 | `projects/04_greek_mythology_monsters/` |\n91: | **Video 5** | Every Type of Bullet Explained | 91 | `projects/05_bullet_types/` |\n92: \n93: > [!NOTE]\n94: > Full deep-dive research for each topic: `niche_research/phase1_part1_topics_1_to_10.md` and `phase1_part2_topics_11_to_20.md`\n95: > Project briefs with production checklists: `projects/[NN]_[name]/project_brief.md`\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## Tool Stack\n100: \n101: ### Research & Scripting\n102: | Tool | Use |\n103: |------|-----|\n104: | NotebookLM | Upload competitor videos, extract insights, gym audio |\n105: | Gemini (web app) | Native video + audio analysis |\n106: | Antigravity IDE | Script writing, research, commands |\n107: | vidIQ (Web App) | Script Writer, Title Generator, Daily Ideas, Learn ONLY |\n108: | vidIQ MCP | Keyword research, outliers, channel stats (5 free accounts) |\n109: \n110: ### Voice & Music\n111: | Tool | Use |\n112: |------|-----|\n113: | ElevenLabs | AI voiceover with emotional tags |\n114: | Google Lyria 3 | Background music matched to scene mood |\n115: \n116: ### Visuals & Assembly\n117: | Tool | Use |\n118: |------|-----|\n119: | Nano Banana 2 | AI image generation |\n120: | Google Omni | AI video clips (2-10 sec) |\n121: | FFmpeg | Local video assembly, audio mixing, 4K export |\n122: | Remotion | React-based programmatic video editing + animated captions |\n123: | GitHub Actions | Free cloud rendering (2,000 min/month) |\n124: \n125: ### Polish\n126: | Tool | Use |\n127: |------|-----|\n128: | CapCut | Captions + color grading |\n129: | Agent Reach | Web scraping for live data |\n130: \n131: ### Script Quality Skills\n132: | Skill | When |\n133: |-------|------|\n134: | `/prompt-forge` | Before writing — creates a rigid, optimized prompt for the AI |\n135: | `/humanizer` | During writing — kills 33 surface AI tells |\n136: | `/ai-writing-gaps` | During writing — fixes 17 structural problems |\n137: | `/stop-slop` | During writing — removes predictable AI prose patterns |\n138: \n139: ### Tool Rules\n140: - Do NOT call vidIQ MCP without permission\n141: - Always mention credit costs before suggesting vidIQ operations\n142: - vidIQ web app: Script Writer, Title Generator, Learn, Daily Ideas ONLY\n143: - Full tool details + setup: `_toolkit/toolkit.md`\n144: \n145: ## vidIQ Integration (What vidIQ Does Better)\n146: \n147: | Pipeline Step | Use vidIQ For | Use Antigravity For |\n148: |---------------|---------------|--------------------|\n149: | Topic validation | Keyword volume + competition scores | Deep topic research + rabbit holes |\n150: | Title | Title scoring (0-100), aim for 85+ | Hook architecture + paradox structure |\n151: | Thumbnail | Scoring + niche benchmarks | Concept design + image generation |\n152: | Tags | Character-counted tag lists with volume data | — |\n153: | Description | Template with timestamps + hashtags | — |\n154: | Post-publish | Retention curves, drop-off analysis, traffic sources | Strategic interpretation of the data |\n155: | Competitor analysis | Live engagement %, VPH, breakout ratios | Forensic analysis of why things work |\n156: \n157: ### Key vidIQ Findings (Aug 19, 2026)\n158: - \"banned weapons explained\" = 0 search vol. Use CTR titles, search-optimized tags.\n159: - \"dark history explained\" = best comp-to-volume ratio (29.1 comp, 13.8K vol)\n160: - \"stickman animation\" = 1.5M monthly volume (huge discovery potential)\n161: - Serious History (819K) = direct stickman competitor, 3.9% engagement\n162: - **⚠️ Feb 1, 2027: Monetization threshold doubles (4K → 8K watch hours)**\n163: - Full vidIQ data: `niche_research/vidiq_data_aug19.md`\n164: \n165: ## Multi-Agent Mode (When Ready)\n166: \n167: Using `/teamwork-preview` in Antigravity, run parallel agents:\n168: - Agent 1: Analyze top 10 channels in your niche via vidIQ\n169: - Agent 2: Research trending keywords\n170: - Agent 3: Build a content calendar\n171: - Agent 4: Clipping research (see clipping/ folder)\n172: \n173: All running simultaneously. Use this AFTER your first video is published, not before.\n174: \n175: ## Daily Schedule Blocks\n176: \n177: | Block | Time | Hours | Use |\n178: |---|---|---|---|\n179: | 🏠 Home Work | ~9-11 AM | 1-2h | Light tasks, planning, prep for library |\n180: | 🚶 Travel | ~11-12 PM | — | To library |\n181: | 📚 Library (Deep Work) | 12-6:45 PM | ~7h | Main work block — laptop + unlimited 5G. Scripting, Remotion, research, production |\n182: | 🏋️ Gym (Passive) | 7-10 PM | 3h | NotebookLM audio + voice notes to WhatsApp \"Capture\" group between sets |\n183: | 🟢 Light Work | 10 PM-12 AM | 1-2h | Progress check, leftover tasks, 3 bullets in WhatsApp \"Daily Log\" at 11:50 PM |\n184: | 🛏️ Sleep | 12 AM | — | Hard cutoff — phone away |\n185: \n186: Total: ~9-10.5h active + 3h passive. 6 working days/week. Thursday = college + REST (library closed).\n187: \n188: > **Current 7-day checklist**: See `7day_checklist_aug11-17.md` for Notion-ready daily tasks.\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: ## Phase 1: Stickman — Production Mode\n193: \n194: **Niche research = COMPLETE.** Deep research for all 20 topics done. Video order decided.\n195: \n196: **Current task:** Produce Video #1 (Every Banned Weapon in History Explained)\n197: 1. Open `projects/01_banned_weapons/project_brief.md`\n198: 2. Follow the production checklist\n199: 3. Use `/prompt-forge` to write the scripting prompt\n200: 4. Deep research already done: `niche_research/phase1_part1_topics_1_to_10.md` → Topic 1\n201: \n202: ---\n203: \n204: ## Phase 1b (Parallel): Nishchay — Study Mode\n205: \n206: **Goal**: Absorb competitor scripting patterns before producing anything.\n207: \n208: **What needs to happen:**\n209: 1. Build a Nishchay competitor database (5-10 channels doing IAS/IPS/DM dramatic content)\n210: 2. Read/analyze their top-performing scripts — dramatic structure, hooks, tension curves\n211: 3. Note what patterns repeat across winning videos\n212: \n213: **This is study time, not production time.** You're sharpening your scripting before you produce.\n214: \n215: **Tools for this:**\n216: - `vidiq_video_transcript` (5 credits) — pull competitor scripts directly\n217: - `vidiq_outliers` (5 credits) — find which videos are outperforming their channel average\n218: - NotebookLM — feed competitor transcripts, generate audio summaries for gym\n219: - Gemini web app — paste video URLs, ask for dramatic structure analysis\n220: \n221: ---\n222: \n223: ## Clipping (Moved to clipping/ folder)\n224: \n225: All clipping details (Whop + Vyro) now live in `clipping/` folder. See:\n226: - `clipping/clipping_overview.md` — overview and TODO\n227: - `clipping/whop/whop_guide.md` — Whop marketplace details\n228: - `clipping/vyro/campaigns.md` — Vyro campaigns and rates\n229: \n230: ---\n231: \n232: ## ADHD Rules (Non-Negotiable)\n233: \n234: 1. **Production before consumption.** No YouTube, no tutorials, no research until the day's production block is done.\n235: 2. **One thing at a time.** Don't start video #2 until video #1 script is done.\n236: 3. **Phone in another room** during deep work.\n237: 4. **If you've been \"planning\" for more than 30 minutes, you're procrastinating.** Start writing.\n238: 5. **No new OneTab saves.** If you find a video, write the title on paper. Review weekly.\n239: \n240: ---\n241: \n242: ## Your Next Action\n243: \n244: **Open `projects/01_banned_weapons/project_brief.md` and start the production checklist.**\n245: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:26:47Z","content":"Now I have the full picture of your workflow. Let me build a comparison that actually matters to YOU.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Personalized AI model comparison transformed for Priyanshu's actual YouTube content creator workflow. Maps generic benchmarks to his real tasks: scriptwriting, ElevenLabs voiceover prep, Remotion code generation, competitor research, thumbnail generation, vidIQ integration, Hindi content for Nishchay Stories, and ADHD-friendly workflow support. Includes custom 'Priyanshu Benchmarks' scoring each model on his actual daily tasks instead of abstract coding/science benchmarks. Covers Opus 4.6, Opus 5, Gemini 3.1 Pro (High), Nemotron 3 Ultra, and OX Alpha.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# AI Model Showdown — For YOUR Workflow, Priyanshu\n\nGeneric benchmarks don't tell you which model writes better scripts, generates better voiceover prep, or handles your Remotion pipeline. This does.\n\n---\n\n## Your Actual Tasks (From Your Agent File + Pipeline)\n\n| # | YOUR Task | What The AI Actually Needs To Do |\n|:---:|---|---|\n| 1 | **Script Writing** (Stikaman + Nishchay) | 1,800-word narrative scripts with hooks, tension curves, pacing |\n| 2 | **Humanizer / Anti-Slop** | Detect and kill AI writing patterns in prose |\n| 3 | **ElevenLabs Voiceover Prep** | Add audio tags, pacing markers, normalize for TTS v3 |\n| 4 | **Research & Fact-Checking** | Deep-dive topics (banned weapons, Greek myths), cite real sources |\n| 5 | **Competitor Analysis** | Analyze competitor transcripts, find outlier patterns |\n| 6 | **Remotion Code** | Write React/TypeScript for programmatic video assembly |\n| 7 | **FFmpeg Commands** | Audio mixing, 4K export, loudness normalization, format conversion |\n| 8 | **Thumbnail Concepts** | Design prompts for Nano Banana 2, visual strategy |\n| 9 | **vidIQ Integration** | Keyword research, title scoring, SEO optimization |\n| 10 | **Hindi Content** (Nishchay) | Hindi scripts, dramatic IAS/IPS narratives |\n| 11 | **Python Scripting** | spy_competitor.py, batch processing, API automation |\n| 12 | **ADHD Task Management** | Short instructions, call out slacking, next 1-2 actions |\n\n---\n\n## Which Benchmark Actually Maps to YOUR Work?\n\nMost benchmarks are **irrelevant to you**. Here's the honest mapping:\n\n| Benchmark | What It Tests | Relevant To You? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **SWE-bench** | Fix GitHub bugs | ⚠️ Somewhat — Remotion/Python debugging |\n| **DeepSWE** | Multi-file coding projects | ⚠️ Somewhat — Remotion builds, pipeline scripts |\n| **MMLU** | General knowledge | ✅ YES — Script research accuracy |\n| **GPQA Diamond** | PhD-level science | ❌ NO — You're not writing physics papers |\n| **HumanEval** | Code from specs | ⚠️ Somewhat — Python/FFmpeg automation |\n| **ARC-AGI-2** | Abstract reasoning | ❌ NO — Irrelevant |\n| **LM Arena (ELO)** | Human preference in conversation | ✅ YES — Writing quality, helpfulness |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **No standard benchmark tests scriptwriting quality, voiceover prep, creative narrative structure, or Hindi content.** These are the things you actually care about. So I'm creating custom ratings based on what each model is known for in practice.\n\n---\n\n## The Priyanshu Benchmark — Models Rated On YOUR Tasks\n\nRating: 🟢 Excellent | 🟡 Good | 🟠 Decent | 🔴 Weak | ❌ Unknown/Untested\n\n### Creative & Content Tasks\n\n| Task | Opus 4.6 | Opus 5 | Gemini 3.1 Pro (High) | Nemotron 3 Ultra | OX Alpha |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **English Script Writing** (hooks, pacing, 1800 words) | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Best | 🟢 Excellent | 🟡 Good | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Hindi Script Writing** (Nishchay dramatic) | 🟢 Strong Hindi | 🟢 Best | 🟡 Good Hindi | 🟠 Weak Hindi | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Humanizer / Kill AI Tells** | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Best | 🟡 Good | 🟠 Decent | ❌ Unknown |\n| **ElevenLabs Voiceover Prep** (audio tags, pacing) | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Excellent | 🟡 Good | 🟠 Decent | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Thumbnail Concept Design** | 🟢 Strong | 🟢 Best | 🟢 Strong | 🟡 Good | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Competitor Script Analysis** | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Best | 🟢 Excellent (1M context!) | 🟡 Good | ❌ Unknown |\n\n### Technical Tasks\n\n| Task | Opus 4.6 | Opus 5 | Gemini 3.1 Pro (High) | Nemotron 3 Ultra | OX Alpha |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **Remotion Code** (React/TS video assembly) | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Best | 🟡 Good | 🟡 Good | 🟠 Decent |\n| **FFmpeg Commands** | 🟢 Reliable | 🟢 Reliable | 🟢 Reliable | 🟡 Good | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Python Automation** (spy_competitor, batch) | 🟢 Strong | 🟢 Best | 🟢 Strong | 🟡 Good | 🟠 Decent |\n| **vidIQ MCP Integration** | 🟢 Works | 🟢 Works | 🟢 Works (native) | 🟠 No MCP | ❌ No MCP |\n| **Debug Broken Scripts** | 🟢 80.8% SWE | 🟢 92%+ SWE | 🟢 80.6% SWE | 🟡 71.9% SWE | ❌ No data |\n\n### Research & Knowledge Tasks\n\n| Task | Opus 4.6 | Opus 5 | Gemini 3.1 Pro (High) | Nemotron 3 Ultra | OX Alpha |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **Topic Research** (banned weapons, Greek myths) | 🟢 87% MMLU | 🟢 92%+ MMLU | 🟢 **92.6% MMLU** | 🟡 88% MMLU | ❌ No data |\n| **Fact-Checking / Source Accuracy** | 🟢 Strong | 🟢 Best | 🟢 Strong | 🟡 Good | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Analyze Full Competitor Channel** (bulk transcripts) | 🟠 200K limit | 🟠 200K limit | 🟢 **1M context — fits everything** | 🟢 1M context | 🟡 1M context but anonymous |\n\n### Workflow & ADHD Support\n\n| Task | Opus 4.6 | Opus 5 | Gemini 3.1 Pro (High) | Nemotron 3 Ultra | OX Alpha |\n|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| **ADHD-Friendly Instructions** (short, direct) | 🟢 Great | 🟢 Great | 🟡 Can be verbose | 🟠 Generic | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Call Out Slacking / Anti-Sycophancy** | 🟢 Excellent | 🟢 Excellent | 🟡 Too polite by default | 🟠 Generic | ❌ Unknown |\n| **Follow Custom Agent Skills** (25+ skills) | 🟢 Works | 🟢 Works | 🟢 Works (native) | ❌ No Antigravity | ❌ No Antigravi